    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n80035" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πατρι-άρχης</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ου</span>,
			ὁ, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πατριἄ</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>father</i> or <i>chief of a
				race, patriarch</i>, <i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>1 Ch.</u>
				27.22
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Act.Ap.</u>
				2.29
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				7.8
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ep.Hebr.</u>
				7.4
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>title borne by the Bishops</i> of Rome, Constantinople,
			Jerusalem, Antioch, and Alexandria, <i><span class="en">
				Just.
				<u>Nov.</u>
				3.2
			</span></i>, etc. :—Adj.
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πατρι-αρχικός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>,
			<i>of</i> or <i>belonging to him</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θρόνος</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				7
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				<u>Praef.</u>
				1
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Cod.Just.</u>
				1.5.12.22
			</span></i>.</div>
